  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA-only models strongly outperform image-only models, multiprofile aggregation improved PCA-based RNA, and scvi_n200 multiprofile models are currently the best performers with validation accuracy around 0.65 and F1 around 0.63. However, there is no singleprofile scvi_n200 result, so it is unclear whether the multiprofile gain is specific to PCA or also holds for the stronger scvi representation. config_004 tests the simpler singleprofile scvi_n200 baseline, isolating the effect of profile setting and aggregation for the currently most promising RNA encoder. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the strong scvi RNA direction without adding a new encoder or modality, clarifies whether multiprofile complexity is necessary, and provides a cleaner basis for later multimodal or fusion comparisons."
}

